                why: "To objectively prioritize which process inputs have the biggest impact on key process outputs.",
                when: "During Measure or Analyze phase, after mapping the process but before detailed data collection.",
                standard: "Ratings: 0 (None), 1 (Low), 3 (Moderate), 9 (Strong).",
                interp: "Inputs with the highest total scores are the Critical X's that likely drive process performance.",
                ref: "Tip: Don't debate scores too long. Focus on relative ranking (Pareto principle).",
                steps: [
                    { title: "1. List Outputs (Y's)", desc: "Identify Key Process Outputs (KPOVs) from customer perspective." },
